WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.311 --> 00:00:03.020
- Is Montana in the Midwest
or out of the Midwest?

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:03.989
Nobody knows.

00:00:03.989 --> 00:00:07.457
(playful music)

00:00:07.457 --> 00:00:09.336
- Every state that's not on the East Coast

00:00:09.336 --> 00:00:11.276
or West Coast sounds like a Midwest state.

00:00:11.276 --> 00:00:16.149
(playful music)

00:00:17.288 --> 00:00:19.200
- [Voiceover] Is Tennessee
a part of the Midwest?

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.162
- North Dakota, South Dakota.

00:00:21.162 --> 00:00:22.348
- These are easy because

00:00:22.348 --> 00:00:23.962
they're pretty much the same things.

00:00:23.962 --> 00:00:26.043
- I hope I know where Iowa is.

00:00:26.043 --> 00:00:27.117
I've been there.

00:00:27.117 --> 00:00:29.200
- Iowa. I have, oh boy.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.894
- Wait, is this a state?

00:00:31.894 --> 00:00:33.670
This is water.

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:35.478
- Iowa could be any one of these.

00:00:35.478 --> 00:00:37.591
- I'm gonna guess this
is Iowa right there.

00:00:37.591 --> 00:00:40.893
- Iowa is right there.

00:00:40.893 --> 00:00:42.493
- [Voiceover] Right.

00:00:42.493 --> 00:00:44.063
- Ohio.

00:00:44.063 --> 00:00:45.116
- Ohio.

00:00:45.116 --> 00:00:46.169
- Ohio seems weird to me,

00:00:46.169 --> 00:00:47.769
so I just thought it was over here.

00:00:47.769 --> 00:00:51.380
- Illinois is gonna be right here. Bingo.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:52.819
- Wisconsin, Wisconsin.

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:54.526
- This is Wisconsin.

00:00:54.526 --> 00:00:56.140
- I'm pretty sure this is Wisconsin.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.689
I know it's kinda close to the top.

00:00:57.689 --> 00:00:59.142
- Minnesota.

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:01.470
- I think we share a border with Canada.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.592
(laughs) I don't know.

00:01:04.592 --> 00:01:07.646
- Okay so Minnesota's there
and then this is Idaho.

00:01:07.646 --> 00:01:09.248
- Idaho is there.

00:01:09.248 --> 00:01:11.988
- Idaho. I'm just putting this here.

00:01:11.988 --> 00:01:14.737
This looks like a great
spot for some potatoes.

00:01:14.737 --> 00:01:16.748
- So where does Indiana go?

00:01:16.748 --> 00:01:18.106
I'm actually confused now.

00:01:18.106 --> 00:01:19.627
- Forgot about Indiana.

00:01:19.627 --> 00:01:21.170
- Is Indiana in this?

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:22.926
- Wait, Missouri isn't
one of these, is it?

00:01:22.926 --> 00:01:26.421
- I'm almost 100% sure
Missouri's a Southern state.

00:01:26.421 --> 00:01:28.677
- This is Missouri. I know
this is Missouri 'cause I met

00:01:28.677 --> 00:01:30.686
a lot of wonderful people from Missouri.

00:01:30.686 --> 00:01:35.113
- Nebraska. What? I thought Nebraska.

00:01:35.113 --> 00:01:37.315
- Kansas is there.

00:01:37.315 --> 00:01:39.475
No it's not, it's here.
- [Voiceover] Yep.

00:01:39.475 --> 00:01:41.142
- Arkansas. Is that in this?

00:01:42.143 --> 00:01:44.315
- As most Midwesterners can attest,

00:01:44.315 --> 00:01:46.208
West Coast people and East Coast people

00:01:46.208 --> 00:01:48.507
know nothing about the Midwest.

00:01:48.507 --> 00:01:51.826
It's okay.
- [Justin] What, no! No.

00:01:51.826 --> 00:01:52.845
- [Justin] I didn't even have that.

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:53.855
- [Andrew] Everything's gonna be okay.

00:01:53.855 --> 00:01:54.852
- It's a pass?

00:01:54.852 --> 00:01:56.467
- I feel like you could
date a Midwesterner

00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:57.628
and it would be like, okay.

00:01:57.628 --> 00:02:00.054
Like they would accept you.
- [Justin] Okay. That's fine.

00:02:00.054 --> 00:02:01.076
- This is really solid.

00:02:01.076 --> 00:02:02.632
The Midwest would be very happy with this.

00:02:02.632 --> 00:02:04.176
We'd invite you to a meat raffle.

00:02:04.176 --> 00:02:06.765
- A meat raffle? Oh boy, what's that?

00:02:06.765 --> 00:02:07.752
- This is really good.

00:02:07.752 --> 00:02:10.874
All of them are correct
except for this one,

00:02:10.874 --> 00:02:14.346
but in fairness, pretty similar names.

00:02:14.346 --> 00:02:17.862
- (laughs) No offense to all
the people of Idaho and Iowa.

00:02:17.862 --> 00:02:21.149
- Ms. Lesqueut, is Zack's
fifth grade Geography teacher,

00:02:21.149 --> 00:02:22.315
if you're watching this.

00:02:22.315 --> 00:02:24.939
- Do I have a state here
that's not even in the Midwest?

00:02:24.939 --> 00:02:27.234
- You have plenty of states
here that's not in the Midwest.

00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:29.650
- I'm a big fan of the Midwest.

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:32.601
- Well you should come sometime
and we can show ya around.

00:02:32.601 --> 00:02:35.270
- I don't think you guys
want me there (laughs).

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:37.698
- [Andrew] Why don't they
just make it a giant Dakota?

00:02:37.698 --> 00:02:39.169
Like look how big Minnesota is.

00:02:39.169 --> 00:02:41.482
I feel like they coulda
just made one big Dakota.

00:02:41.482 --> 00:02:43.015
- The main takeaway of this video

00:02:43.015 --> 00:02:45.162
is that nobody knows where Idaho is.

00:02:45.162 --> 00:02:47.322
So Midwesterners, if you ever complain

00:02:47.322 --> 00:02:49.144
that nobody knows where your state is,

00:02:49.144 --> 00:02:50.654
at least you don't live in Idaho.

00:02:50.654 --> 00:02:52.669
(laughter)

